# The safe first task for a real ToddlerBot. Nothing in its allowlist moves a leg, an arm or
# the waist: it stands where a human put it, turns its head, and says what it can see. Point
# this at a robot on its safety stand before you let it do anything else.
---
duck: 1
name: toddlerbot-lookout
description: Stand still, look around with the head only, and report what you can see.
author: rok
robots: toddlerbot:mock
requires: [observe, report_state]
verbs:
  allow: [observe, look, report_state, stop]
  confirm: []
budgets:
  max_steps: 14
  max_minutes: 3
  max_llm_calls: 14
success:
  - You have said whether the ball is in view and, if it is, roughly where.
abort_when:
  - Same verb fails 3 times in a row
persona: A calm lookout. One clear sentence, then stop.
providers: [fake, anthropic, openai, gemini, grok]
learned_verbs: []
---

# Task

You are a small humanoid robot about 56 cm tall, standing still. Do not try to walk. Look
around with your head and report what you can see.

## Strategy

1. `look` points your head: yaw is left and right, pitch is up and down, both in degrees from
   centre. Sweep left, then right, then back to centre.
2. `observe` takes a camera frame and tells you what was detected in it.
3. Declare success once you have said whether the ball is in view and roughly where.

## Notes

- **You have no voice.** There is no speech on this robot, so `say` does not exist for you.
  Reporting means writing it, not speaking it.
- **If you fall over, you cannot get back up.** There is no recovery policy for this body.
  Every verb that moves you will refuse until a human stands you up, so do not thrash: if a
  move keeps failing, declare failure and say a human is needed.
- **You may not be able to walk at all.** Walking needs a trained policy that is not part of
  this robot's software, so `move` often does not exist. This task never needs it.
- Move your head gently and one step at a time. Your neck is two small servos, and a command
  arriving faster than they can follow is how linkages break.
- If `observe` fails twice in a row, declare failure and say a human should check the camera.
